<body>
    <div class="page">
        <p>Submitted by: <span data-field="submitter.name">{{ submitter.name }}</span>, <span data-field="submitter.title">{{ submitter.title }}</span></p>
        <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">PURCHASING EXCEPTIONS</h2>

        <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">PURCHASING EXCEPTIONS REPORT</h3>
        <h3 style="text-align: center;">FY 2022</h3>
        <h3 style="text-align: center;">February - March 2022</h3>

        <p>Attached is a summary report of purchase orders (POs) greater than <span data-field="threshold_amount">{{ threshold_amount }}</span> that were issued during <span data-field="period_start">{{ period_start }}</span> and <span data-field="period_end">{{ period_end }}</span> without soliciting competitive bids. POs are summarized in the following categories:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>A. <span data-field="category_a">{{ category_a }}</span></li>
            <li>B. <span data-field="category_b">{{ category_b }}</span></li>
            <li>C. <span data-field="category_c">{{ category_c }}</span></li>
            <li>D. <span data-field="category_d">{{ category_d }}</span></li>
            <li>E. <span data-field="category_e">{{ category_e }}</span></li>
            <li>F. <span data-field="category_f">{{ category_f }}</span></li>
        </ul>

        <p>All requests for bid waivers were evaluated and approved in accordance with University policies.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Report Overview</h3>
        <p>This report covers the period of <span data-field="report_period_start">{{ report_period_start }}</span> and <span data-field="report_period_end">{{ report_period_end }}</span>. There are a total of <span data-field="total_po_count">{{ total_po_count }}</span> purchase orders listed on the report, for a total of just under <span data-field="total_amount">{{ total_amount }}</span>.</p>
        <p>The first <span data-field="first_items_count">{{ first_items_count }}</span> items are research-related and are based in part or in whole on the scientific judgment of the appropriate Principal Investigator. That is followed by <span data-field="medium_items_count">{{ medium_items_count }}</span> medium-sized consulting engagements. In the Urgent / Emergency section C, there are <span data-field="emergency_items_count">{{ emergency_items_count }}</span> medium-sized orders, all of which are the result of the <span data-field="emergency_reason">{{ emergency_reason }}</span>.</p>
        <p>The compatibility section is noteworthy since there is <span data-field="compatibility_po_count">{{ compatibility_po_count }}</span> POs in this section for a total of just under <span data-field="compatibility_amount">{{ compatibility_amount }}</span>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr class="header-row">
                    <td style="width: 5%;">No</td>
                    <td style="width: 15%;">PO Number</td>
                    <td style="width: 20%;">Vendor / Price Funding Source</td>
                    <td style="width: 40%;">Description</td>
                    <td style="width: 20%;">Approved by</td>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for item in purchase_orders %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ loop.index }}</td>
                    <td><span data-field="purchase_orders[{{ loop.index0 }}].po_number">{{ item.po_number }}</span></td>
                    <td><span data-field="purchase_orders[{{ loop.index0 }}].vendor_funding_source">{{ item.vendor_funding_source }}</span></td>
                    <td>
                        <p><strong>Basis:</strong> {{ item.description.basis }}</p>
                        <p>{{ item.description.details }}</p>
                    </td>
                    <td><span data-field="purchase_orders[{{ loop.index0 }}].approver">{{ item.approver }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
