        <td>
          <p>Basis: Recommended Source for Specialty Training Services</p>
          <p>Critical Incident Stress Management (CISM) & Advanced Trainings for frontline workers in response to critical incidents. This is a continuation of services provided by the Michigan Crisis Response Association.</p>
          <p>Grant Funds - Psychiatry</p>
          <p>This is a very specialized training and MCRA is the only MI based organization that provides the accredited CISM training. Trainings are also held by ICISF faculty, but ICISF does not have the accreditation for CISM. MCRA is the only organization in Michigan that provides the accredited CISM training. The response was highly satisfactory. Our team has a great relationship with the MCRA trainers and the response for additional trainings has soared.</p>
          <p>The trainers at MCRA are certified in CISM. The process to get certification is time consuming and expensive. We have utilized MCRA for several years, and the trainers are highly knowledgeable and experienced. Not only were the ICISF prices higher, but they did not have the scheduling flexibility that MCRA had. We have been very satisfied with the services provided by MCRA.</p>
          <p>This is a highly specific training accreditation for individuals working in areas with trauma exposure. Because the department has several faculty that specialize in stress, anxiety and trauma, the department did the leg work on finding the best organization to provide this training.</p>
        </td>
        <td class="right-align">
          <p>Jennifer Ballard - Director for Psychiatry and Behavioral Neurosciences,</p>
          <p>approved by Kenneth Doherty</p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
